{
  "$comment": "Every website image slot. The renderer uses a slot's own files only when status is 'implemented'; otherwise it shows the named fallback from 'library', or a neutral placeholder where the layout requires one. Process supplied images with: npm run images:process -- <slot> <file>. Prompts and validation criteria: docs/IMAGE-PRODUCTION-QUEUE.md. 'focal' and 'fallbackFocal' are CSS object-position percentages (0 = align left/top edge, 1 = right/bottom), not the subject's coordinates: a subject at 60% across a 3:2 image needs about 0.75 to stay centred in a square crop.",
